  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Elevated blood pressure at a pre-expedition medical assessment, 144/90 mmHg in the office without symptoms; hypertension not yet confirmed; one week of home readings requested</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding at the pre-expedition assessment; no blood pressure from his lifetime is known. Superseded at the second visit by the confirmed diagnosis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Nicotine dependence, pipe tobacco: about 25 g a week since his early twenties; first pipe within an hour of waking; has never tried to stop</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F17.290</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding anchored to his documented tobacco use on a sledge journey; the amount and pattern are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Personal history of scurvy on a long polar sledge journey in his mid-thirties, with red gums and swollen ankles and legs, treated with fresh seal meat, and full recovery; months on preserved food again ahead</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
