<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Wilderness and expedition medicine consultation in two weeks to assess fitness for a long polar expedition and to plan nutrition, cold-injury and altitude precautions, mental health support, and evacuation. Guideline: Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Prevention and Treatment of Frostbite: 2024 Update (McIntosh SE, et al. Wilderness Environ Med 2024;35(2):183-197) (2024); Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Out-of-Hospital Evaluation and Treatment of Accidental Hypothermia: 2019 Update (Dow J, et al. Wilderness Environ Med 2019;30(4S):S47-S69) (2019) [S]</item><item>Confirm the blood pressure with a validated upper-arm home monitor, two readings morning and evening for seven days, and start lifestyle measures: less salt, more fruit and vegetables, regular endurance training, and alcohol within limits. Guideline: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Circulation 2025;152(11):e114-e218) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Stop pipe tobacco: varenicline with a quit date in one week, counseling at each visit, and the quitline; nicotine products avoided because nicotine narrows skin blood vessels and adds to frostbite risk. Guideline: Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Prevention and Treatment of Frostbite: 2024 Update (McIntosh SE, et al. Wilderness Environ Med 2024;35(2):183-197) (2024); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021) [S]</item><item>Baseline PHQ-9 and GAD-7 before a long isolated expedition, repeated before departure, with a mental health and sleep support plan. Guideline: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023); Anxiety Disorders in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item>Dental examination and cleaning, pure-tone audiometry, and an eye examination with a spare pair of glasses before departure. Guideline: USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
